    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `namesakeCount` feature on owner creation. When an owner is created via `POST /api/owners`, the response and subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}` now return `namesakeCount` = the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same first and last name, compared case-insensitively.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `namesakeCount` (integer, minimum 0) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persisted `Integer namesakeCount` field (`namesake_count` column) with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it to the DTO automatically by name.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Computes the count via a new `countNamesakes(firstName, lastName)` helper that streams existing owners (`clinicService.findAllOwners()`, which excludes the not-yet-saved owner) and counts case-insensitive first+last name matches, then sets it on the owner before saving.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `namesake_count` column. The test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so this column addition is what makes persistence work.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCountsNamesakes` (two owners sharing \"Ann\"/surname \u2192 second owner gets `namesakeCount = 1`) passes, and the full suite is green.",
